    "identifier": "knock-back",
    "description": "<p>When you hit a creature with an attack, you can spend a superiority die. When you do, you push the target in a direction away from you. They move a number of feet away equal to 10 x the result of the superiority Die and end this movement falling prone. If your movement would be stopped by a structure no thicker than 5 feet, then structure is destroyed and they continue their movement taking 2d6 bludgeoning damage for each structure they pass through.</p>",
